.TH "PKGSOURCE_RECIPE_YAML" "5" "" "libpkgsource\-yaml 1.0.0" "libpkgsource\-yaml"
.SH NAME
pkgsource_recipe_yaml \- describe the native recipe YAML version 1 protocol
.SH DESCRIPTION
A \f[CR]zeppe\-lin.recipe/1\f[R] document declares one package release.
Its root contains required \f[CR]format\f[R], \f[CR]package\f[R], \f[CR]requirements\f[R], \f[CR]sources\f[R], and \f[CR]build\f[R] values, plus optional \f[CR]check\f[R], \f[CR]lifecycle\f[R], and \f[CR]architectures\f[R] values.
.PP
This first published protocol includes the optional check program.
There is no published recipe/2 compatibility generation.
.PP
Requirements use explicit \f[CR]package\f[R] or \f[CR]profile\f[R] subject mappings and retain separate build, run, check, and action\-bound lifecycle scopes.
Sources contain exactly one \f[CR]url\f[R] or \f[CR]path\f[R], plus explicit \f[CR]name\f[R] and lowercase SHA\-256 fields.
Programs contain exact \f[CR]language: posix\-shell\f[R] and \f[CR]script\f[R] fields.
.SH AUTHORITY
The parser returns one \f[CR]recipe_declaration\f[R].
It does not seal profiles or source authority, open files, fetch inputs, execute programs, resolve requirements, or construct plans.
.PP
The caller passes the declaration and one explicit sealed profile catalog to \f[CR]seal_source()\f[R].
That core operation owns profile expansion, normalization, duplicate detection, lifecycle and check\-program binding, and source identity.
.SH YAML CONTRACT
Exactly one strict YAML document is accepted.
Directives, anchors, aliases, merge keys, custom or incompatible tags, duplicate keys, complex mapping keys, unknown schema keys, scalar requirement shorthand, and type drift are rejected.
Parser resource limits apply.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]pkgsource_yaml(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_profiles_yaml(5)\f[R]
